Feature: Mask Invoice Number in Product Revenue Clone Table

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog schema is purgo_playground
    And the original table is purgo_databricks.purgo_playground.d_product_revenue
    And a clone table for processing is purgo_databricks.purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone

  Scenario: Setup clone table for processing
    Given the clone table purgo_databricks.purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone exists
      And it should be dropped to ensure a clean state
    When a new clone table is created from d_product_revenue
    Then the schema and data should replicate the source table

  Scenario Outline: Mask invoice number in clone table
    Given the field invoice_number in the clone table is of type <data_type>
    When applying the PySpark logic to mask the last 4 digits
    Then the invoice_number should appear as '123423****' for the example '1234234534'
      And masked values should be saved back to purgo_databricks.purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone

    Examples:
      | data_type |
      | bigint    |
      | string    |

  Scenario: Validate the masking logic
    Given a non-empty invoice_number field in the clone table
    When verifying masking logic
    Then no invoice_number should retain its original form
      And masked invoice_numbers should end with '****'

  Scenario Outline: Handle erroneous data and failure cases
    Given the invoice_number contains <erroneous_data>
    When attempting to mask the invoice_number
    Then the operation should fail gracefully 
      And log an error message <error_message>

    Examples:
      | erroneous_data | error_message                           |
      | null           | "Invoice number cannot be null."        |
      | negative value | "Invoice number must be a positive."    |
      | non-numeric    | "Invoice number must contain digits."   |

  Scenario: Verify rollback on failure
    Given a scenario where masking operation fails due to invalid data
    When the rollback is triggered
    Then the clone table should maintain the integrity of original data

  Scenario: Ensure logging and error tracing 
    Given the masking logic is in operation
    When an error occurs
    Then detailed logs should capture the failure point
      And alerts should be sent to the data engineering team
